	"web_text": "From \"Turkoman Rugs,\" Fogg Art Museum, Harvard, exhibition cat. pg. 47: \"This rug shows many non-Turkoman features. The hanging poemegranates and stylized flowers of the design and the yellow color appearing on the border reveal the influence of the rugs of Chinese Turkestan. The form of the prayer niche is like no other found on Turkoman rugs, but is reminiscent of certain Turkish prayer rugs. The weave is loose. The wool is softer and more silky than the wool of most Turkoman rugs.\"",
	"didactic_label": null,
	"exhibition_history_text": "January 26 - March 6, 1966: Fogg Art Museum, Cambridge, MA. \n \"Turoman Rugs.\" (catalogue noted in \"Publications field.\"\nFor Tent & Trade: Masterpieces of Turkmen Weaving, 2007-2008",
